                <p style="text-align: center; color: #666; margin-bottom: 3rem;">Find solutions to common IT problems and learn how to fix minor issues yourself.</p>
                
                <div class="knowledge-base cards">
                    <div class="kb-category">
                        <div class="card-top">
                            <img src="https://i.pcmag.com/imagery/roundups/03vMLiY0vu25u3uAUqohe98-1..v1569492680.jpg" alt="Blog Name">
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-info">
                        <h3>Data Recovery</h3>
                        <span class="date">Monday, Jan 20, 2021</span>
                        <p class="excerpt">If you accidentally deleted a file, don’t panic. First, check your Recycle Bin. If it’s not there, try free recovery tools like Recuva or EaseUS. For best results, stop using the drive immediately to avoid overwriting lost data.
                        </p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-bottom flex-row">
                            <a href="#" class="read-more">Watch Full Blog</a>
                            <a href="#" class="button btn-yellow">Channel</a>
                        </div>
                    </div>
    
                    <div class="kb-category">
                        <div class="card-top">
                            <img src="https://www.man-sys.co.uk/wp-content/uploads/2019/12/computer-maintenance.png" alt="Blog Name" alt="Blog Name">
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-info">
                        <h3>Maintenance Tips</h3>
                        <span class="date">Monday, Jan 20, 2021</span>
                        <p class="excerpt">To keep your computer working well, clean up old files, uninstall programs you don’t use, and restart it often. Also, install system updates regularly — they fix bugs and improve performance.</p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-bottom flex-row">
                            <a href="#" class="read-more">Watch Full Blog</a>
                            <a href="#" class="button btn-yellow">Channel</a>
                        </div>
                    </div>
    
                    <div class="kb-category">
                        <div class="card-top">
                            <img src="https://nahil.com.sa/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/%D8%AA%D9%88%D8%A7%D8%AC%D9%87-%D8%A8%D8%B7%D8%A1-%D9%81%D9%8A-%D8%AC%D9%87%D8%A7%D8%B2-%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%83%D9%85%D8%A8%D9%8A%D9%88%D8%AA%D8%B1%D8%9F-%D8%A5%D9%84%D9%8A%D9%83-%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%AD%D9%84-1024x569.jpg" alt="Blog Name">
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-info">
                        <h3>Slow Computer Performance</h3>
                        <span class="date">Monday, Jan 20, 2021</span>
                        <p class="excerpt">A slow computer usually means too many apps running, low memory, or even a virus. Close extra programs, run a virus scan, and check if your disk is almost full. Restarting your device also helps.</p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-bottom flex-row">
                            <a href="#" class="read-more">Watch Full Blog</a>
                            <a href="#" class="button btn-yellow">Channel</a>
                        </div>
                    </div>
    
                    <div class="kb-category">
                        <div class="card-top">
                            <img src="https://www.australiancomputertraders.com.au/assets/images/Windows%20BSOD%20Image.jpg" alt="Blog Name">
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-info">
                        <h3>Blue Screen Errors (BSOD)</h3>
                        <span class="date">Monday, Jan 20, 2021</span>
                        <p class="excerpt">A blue screen usually means your computer had a serious error. Write down the error code, then search what it means. Often it’s caused by a driver issue or a hardware problem. Restart and check for updates.</p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-bottom flex-row">
                            <a href="#" class="read-more">Watch Full Blog</a>
                            <a href="#" class="button btn-yellow">Channel</a>
                        </div>
                    </div>
    
                    <div class="kb-category">
                        <div class="card-top">
                            <img src="https://getquicktech.com.au/wp-content/uploads/2020/09/Peripheral-Setup-Troubleshoot-and-Repair_01.jpg" alt="Blog Name">
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-info">
                        <h3>Printer & Peripheral Setup</h3>
                        <span class="date">Monday, Jan 20, 2021</span>
                        <p class="excerpt">Make sure your printer or device is connected properly. Then install the right driver from the company’s website. If it still doesn’t work, try restarting both your PC and the printer.</p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-bottom flex-row">
                            <a href="#" class="read-more">Watch Full Blog</a>
                            <a href="#" class="button btn-yellow">Channel</a>
                        </div>
                    </div>
    
                    <div class="kb-category">
                        <div class="card-top">
                            <img src="https://i.pcmag.com/imagery/roundups/00IBj7QgR0HtuwfikyDdyTq-12..v1616705579.png" alt="Blog Name">
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-info">
                        <h3>Backup Solutions</h3>
                        <span class="date">Monday, Jan 20, 2021</span>
                        <p class="excerpt">Backing up means saving a copy of your important files. You can use a USB drive, an external hard disk, or cloud storage like Google Drive. This way, even if your device breaks, your data stays safe.</p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="card-bottom flex-row">
